{
  "version": 1,
  "_about": [
    "Interior plans for building types, read by engine/interior_gen.py (task-567).",
    "",
    "A plan is drawn, not coded: `plan` is a list of rows of one-character tokens",
    "and `legend` maps each token to a biome id (or null for an empty cell). The",
    "result is painted into the child scope's grid as ordinary cells, so the",
    "standard compiler (task-496) builds the areas, the doorways, the merge rules",
    "(task-564) and the descriptions. The generator mints no areas of its own,",
    "which is why an author can edit a generated interior by editing paint.",
    "",
    "Token conventions used by most plans: `=` is a wall, so is the outside of the",
    "plan; a space is a door; a digit counts 1-9 storeys (a stair cell also needs",
    "to be in the legend, or it will not be a place).",
    "",
    "`repeat_storeys` reuses `plan` on every storey above the first, which is what",
    "an apartment block or a keep is: the same plan, stacked. `storeys` is the",
    "default height when the caller does not say otherwise; a building with a",
    "generator ignores it and says so in its report."
  ],
